{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$verdict = @'\"'\nReviewed: 6701eec3831f5b3b5d18a61a765caa52dc540768\n\nVerified: Independently reviewed the prescribed three-dot diff, WI-978 and its item-16 spec target/quoted owner ruling, PROCESS sections 3–6, the review rubric, and targeted current/historical requirement rows. Reservation, record preservation, ordinary landing-table, and fold cases passed in the prescribed run. Eight selected regressions failed against the base behavior. The worktree remains unchanged. The admission bypass below was reproduced through both shipped landing callers, including a successful integrate_one flow.\n\nCommands (Python below is C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe):\n\n- \"'`git rev-parse HEAD` -> `6701eec3831f5b3b5d18a61a765caa52dc540768`.\n- `git diff c6e982882e81b7369bd4ca323ad1e06ebe93b108...6701eec3831f5b3b5d18a61a765caa52dc540768 -- . '\"':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'\"'` (also name/stat and focused path reads); `Get-Content`, `Select-Object`, and `rg` targeted guidance/spec/registry/source reads -> reviewed authored changes and generated catalogue digest; no implementer session assessment used. Registry reads in the review were targeted to cited rows.\n- With `$env:GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES = '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-01d-leg29'\"'`: `& '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n 2 --basetemp 'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-01d-leg29/r1-978-A/wi-978' 'tests/test_id_watermark.py' 'tests/test_id_carrier.py' 'tests/test_id_carrier_git.py' 'tests/test_id_landing.py' 'tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py' 'tests/test_held_status_git.py' 'tests/test_import_layers.py' 'tests/test_integrate_admission.py' 'tests/test_integrate.py' 'tests/test_plan_gate.py' 'tests/test_pre_commit_hook.py' 'tests/test_rejudge.py' 'tests/test_prompts.py' 'tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py' 'tests/test_dogfood_sync.py'\"'` -> `20 failed, 672 passed, 1 skipped in 783.51s (0:13:03)`.\n- `& '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' project-trajectory/scripts/check_trajectory.py --strict\"'` -> `check_trajectory: clean (986 work item(s), 872 done (88%), 34 cancelled, graph acyclic).`\n- `& '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py --strict-integrity | Select-Object -Last 1\"'` -> `Traceability: SN=31 SR=138 LLR=329 TC=356 orphans=0 integrity=0 verified-mechanized=131 verified-demonstrated=7 verified-attested=0 drafts=4 budgets=4 budget-findings=0 components=4 component-findings=0 interfaces=255 interface-findings=0 ac-advisories=1 paraphrase-advisories=2. Report -> docs'\"\\\\test\\\\report.md\"'`.\n- Python preparation using `git archive c6e982882e81b7369bd4ca323ad1e06ebe93b108 project-trajectory/scripts tests`, tar extraction under the authorized review directory, and copying the reviewed conftest/regression tests over that base -> isolated pre-fix code, no checkout change. Pytest with `-q -p no:cacheprovider --basetemp '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-01d-leg29/r1-978-A/red-before-tmp'\"'` on `test_bump_ids_keeps_every_reservation_record`, `test_correct_mark_keeps_every_reservation_record`, `test_sequential_reservations_are_disjoint`, and `test_the_slot_refuses_each_unreserved_landing[another-wis-record]` -> `4 failed, 2 warnings in 17.96s`. Both writers dropped records; the reserve verb was absent; the old slot admitted the other work item'\"'s identity.\n- Pre-fix pytest with \"'`-q -p no:cacheprovider --tb=short --basetemp '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-01d-leg29/r1-978-A/red-record-tmp'\"'` on `test_a_rise_covered_by_a_reservation_record_passes`, `test_an_altered_committed_record_is_refused`, `test_a_deleted_committed_record_is_refused`, and `test_a_merge_dropping_one_parents_record_is_refused` -> `4 failed, 1 warning in 5.32s`. The old rule refused a justified reservation rise and accepted alteration/deletion of committed records.\n- Extracted the complete base `project-trajectory` with `git archive`; ran the unchanged base `tests/test_pre_commit_hook.py` with `-q -p no:cacheprovider --tb=line --basetemp '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-01d-leg29/r1-978-A/base-hooks-tmp'\"'` -> `19 failed, 12 passed, 1 warning in 151.42s (0:02:31)`. These are the same 19 hook failures as at the reviewed tip: Git Bash terminates with `CreateFileMapping ... Win32 error 5` before executing the hook. They are not lane findings. The twentieth tip failure is the new sweep-equivalence test'\"'s \"'`git add` receiving `insufficient permission for adding an object to repository database C:/Projects/ai-template/.git/objects`; its private index does not isolate the object database. The sweep assertion therefore remains unexecuted here, rather than establishing a code regression.\n- Inline Python probes constructed real claimed-lane repositories under this review directory using the landing suite'\"'s fixtures. With ordinary \"'`.gitattributes` content `docs/requirements/** export-ignore`, the working sweep found `[('\"'SR', 6)]\"'`, the staged sweep returned `[]`, the hand squash `reserved-ids` step exited 0, and the merge-slot admission rung returned None. Initial full-slot follow-ups encountered fixture setup errors (wrong repository path, then inherited loop provenance); these were corrected, not treated as product evidence.\n- `& '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-01d-leg29/r1-978-A/archive_probe.py\"'` -> the fresh, correctly isolated full-slot reproduction printed `branch added SR ids: []`, `merge-slot: None`, `landed: True`, `carrier: None`; integrate_one refreshed, merge